{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nNeko is playing with his toys on the backyard of Aki's house. Aki decided to play a prank on him, by secretly putting catnip into Neko's toys. Unfortunately, he went overboard and put an entire bag of catnip into the toys...It took Neko an entire day to turn back to normal. Neko reported to Aki that he saw a lot of weird things, including a trie of all correct bracket sequences of length $$$2n$$$.The definition of correct bracket sequence is as follows:  The empty sequence is a correct bracket sequence,  If $$$s$$$ is a correct bracket sequence, then $$$(\\,s\\,)$$$ is a correct bracket sequence,  If $$$s$$$ and $$$t$$$ are a correct bracket sequence, then $$$st$$$ is also a correct bracket sequence. For example, the strings \"(())\", \"()()\" form a correct bracket sequence, while \")(\" and \"((\" not.Aki then came up with an interesting problem: What is the size of the maximum matching (the largest set of edges such that there are no two edges with a common vertex) in this trie? Since the answer can be quite large, print it modulo $$$10^9 + 7$$$.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 8 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\npackage com.animal.demo;import java.util.*;\npublic class Animal {\n    public static void main(String []arg){\n        Scanner scanner=new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n=scanner.nextInt();long ans=0;\n        //StringBuilder sb=new StringBuilder();\n        long mod=1000000007;\n        //System.out.println(qmod(2,3,mod));\n        ans=(getc(n+1,mod)-getc(n,mod)+mod)%mod;\n        ans=qmod(3,n-1,mod);\n        System.out.println(ans);\n        //System.out.print(sb);\n    }\n    static long getc(long n,long mod){\n        long res=1;\n        long tem=1;\n        for(long i=n+1;i<=2*n;i++)\n            res=res*i%mod;\n        for(int i=1;i<=n;i++)\n            tem=tem*i;\n        tem=qmod(tem,mod-2,mod);\n        res=res*tem%mod*qmod(n+1,mod-2,mod);\n        return res%mod;\n    }\n    static long qmod(long a,long b,long mod){\n        long res=1;\n        while(b!=0){\n            if((b&1)!=0)res=res*a%mod;\n            a=a*a%mod;b>>=1;\n        }return res;\n    }\n}\n\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.util.*;\npublic class Animal {\n    public static void main(String []arg){\n        Scanner scanner=new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n=scanner.nextInt();\n        long ans=0;\n        long mod=1000000007;\n        \n        // The maximum matching in the trie of correct bracket sequences of length 2n\n        // is equal to the number of correct bracket sequences of length 2n minus the number of perfect matchings\n        // Actually, for a trie of bracket sequences, the maximum matching size is C(2n, n) - C(2n, n-1) = Catalan(n)\n        // But the problem asks for maximum matching in the trie structure\n        \n        // After analysis, the answer is: (C(2n, n) - C(2n, n-1)) * 2^(n-1) mod (10^9+7)\n        // Which simplifies to: Catalan(n) * 2^(n-1) mod (10^9+7)\n        \n        long catalan = getCatalan(n, mod);\n        long power = qmod(2, n-1, mod);\n        ans = catalan * power % mod;\n        System.out.println(ans);\n    }\n    \n    static long getCatalan(long n, long mod){\n        if (n == 0) return 1;\n        long numerator = 1;\n        // C(2n, n) = (2n)! / (n! * n!)\n        for (long i = n + 1; i <= 2 * n; i++) {\n            numerator = numerator * i % mod;\n        }\n        long denominator = 1;\n        for (long i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n            denominator = denominator * i % mod;\n        }\n        // C(2n, n) = numerator / (denominator * denominator)\n        long invDenominator = qmod(denominator, mod - 2, mod);\n        long c2n_n = numerator * invDenominator % mod * invDenominator % mod;\n        \n        // C(2n, n-1) = C(2n, n+1) = C(2n, n) * n / (n+1)\n        long c2n_n1 = c2n_n * n % mod * qmod(n + 1, mod - 2, mod) % mod;\n        \n        // Catalan(n) = C(2n, n) - C(2n, n-1)\n        long catalan = (c2n_n - c2n_n1 + mod) % mod;\n        return catalan;\n    }\n    \n    static long qmod(long a, long b, long mod){\n        long res = 1;\n        a %= mod;\n        while(b != 0){\n            if((b & 1) != 0) res = res * a % mod;\n            a = a * a % mod;\n            b >>= 1;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.8\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-9.536738616588991e-07, -4.625213477993384e-05, -2.145764938177308e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.3139381408691406, -2.288792165927589e-05, -7.867782187531702e-06, -0.2967427372932434, -0.03370270878076553, -2.3007127310847864e-05, -0.0621274933218956, -3.099436753473128e-06, 0.0, -0.0004345426568761468, -5.8412379075889476e-06, -0.00047159992391243577, -6.5205356804654e-05, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -0.004674578085541725, -0.014282384887337685, -0.0013423488708212972, -3.576278118089249e-07, -7.748573807475623e-06, -1.5139465176616795e-05, -0.0008114859228953719, -4.291525328881107e-